 ## How amounts are stored
 
-Whenever you add an expense, tally converts the amount into US dollars using the
-conversion table in `tally/rates.py` and stores that dollar figure. The original
-amount and currency you typed are kept alongside it for reference, but every total
-you ever see is computed in US dollars. This keeps reports consistent even when a
-month mixes several currencies.
+Amounts are stored in whatever currency you entered them in. Each record keeps your
+original amount and currency code exactly as you typed them. Alongside that, tally
+also records a USD equivalent (derived from the conversion table in `tally/rates.py`)
+so that totals and averages can be summed consistently when a month mixes several
+currencies. The displayed totals use that USD figure, but your original amounts are
+never discarded or overwritten.
 
